1. Project structure
.
├── ansible/
├── app.Dockerfile
├── jenkins/
│   ├── jenkins.Dockerfile
│   ├── plugins.txt
│   └── jenkins_build_deploy.groovy
├── pom.xml
├── src/
├── target/
└── terraform/


2. Description of jenkins folder contents

-   jenkins.Dockerfile - Dockerfile for building Jenkins image with required plugins and dependencies.
-   plugins.txt - list of Jenkins plugins that are installed when building the image.
-   jenkins_build_deploy.groovy - Pipeline script for building, fluffing and deploying the application.


3. Run Jenkins in Docker

a. Go to the jenkins/ folder:

    cd jenkins

b. Put together an image of Jenkins:

    docker build -t custom-jenkins -f jenkins.Dockerfile 

c. Start a Jenkins container (example):

    docker run -d -p 8080:8080 -p 50000:50000 --name jenkins custom-jenkins

d. Open it in your browser: http://<docker_host_ip>:8080


4. How to use pipeline jenkins_build_deploy.groovy

-   In Jenkins, create a new pipeline job.
-   Specify the contents of jenkins_build_deploy.groovy as the pipeline script.
-   Make sure to configure for correct operation:
-   AWS Credentials (aws-ecr-creds) with ECR permissions.
-   SSH key (tomcat-ssh-key) to access the Tomcat server.


5. Configuring the Jenkins environment

-   The Dockerfile is already prescribed to install the required plugins from plugins.txt.
-   Make sure that all plugins are specified in plugins.txt, for example:
blueocean:1.27.19
workflow-aggregator
credentials-binding
docker-workflow
ansible
git
terraform
aws-credentials
pipeline-aws
locale
dark-theme
pipeline-stage-view
docker-plugin
matrix-auth
timestamper
publish-over-ssh
maven-plugin


6. Recommendations for working with Jenkins and Ansible
-   In the Jenkins pipeline, you can run ansible playbooks to automate deployment.
-   To do this, you can add a stage with a shell command run, such as:

  stage('Deploy via Ansible') {
    steps {
      sh 'ansible-playbook -i inventory/hosts.ini ansible/playbook.yml'
    }
  }
  -   Ensure the Jenkins agent has access to the right keys and inventories.


7. Example command for manual build and deploy (if needed)

-    docker build -t custom-jenkins -f jenkins/jenkins.Dockerfile .
-    docker run -d -p 8080:8080 -p 50000:50000 --name jenkins custom-jenkins
